1. The build's drawing rule (publishing/edition.py, unsafe_svg) now takes your 010 and 011 terms. An href is allowed only when the whole attribute is data:image/png, data:image/jpeg or data:image/webp in base64. The base64 must decode strictly, and the bytes must carry that type's signature (for WebP, RIFF and WEBP). Every other href is refused: http, xlink to anything else, a fragment, svg+xml, text/html, or an unquoted one. Script, handler, foreignObject, @import and any url() other than an internal #id are refused too, and a drawing over 8 MB. Tested on eight cases. No drawing placed before is newly refused. Placed under it: ruv-sgit's three-rounds.svg (the seventy, chapter 7) and three-frames.svg (the full book, chapter 1), both of which you checked.
2. Screenshot kinds: index and motion added; team stays refused until a cropped copy exists and you have read it.
